# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` checks the 336
# tracked *.sh files out with CRLF. Git Bash tolerates the trailing \r in a
# shebang; WSL and real Linux do not — `./setup` there dies with
# `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` (exit 127). A Windows
# clone must therefore be runnable from whichever shell the consumer has.
#
# `text=auto` leaves detected-binary files (demo/*.gif) alone.
# Form matches prettier and lint-staged (both ship exactly this single line).
* text=auto eol=lf
